```
ROLE: product_realist  VOTE: red
REAL_USE_CASE: Teams serving high-QPS agentic tool-calling (JSON scaffolding, schema keys, delimiters) could use early-exit, but they should deploy a single best-tuned global threshold; the structure-aware per-class tau adds no operational value.
OPERATIONAL_SIGNIFICANCE: Microbenchmark-only. Structure-aware per-class saves only +0.46pp FLOPs over best-tuned global at realistic f (0.2-0.3), median +0.42pp, max +1.17pp; 0/90 swept configs clear the pre-registered 5pp bar (max 1.52pp at f=0.5). Best-tuned global already saves ~10.8% FLOPs; structure-aware reaches ~11.3% — the 0.5pp sliver is noise (struct_flop_sd ≤0.0043) and would vanish under real wall-clock overhead (intermediate-head compute, batched-exit raggedness, KV-cache implications) flagged in LIMITATIONS #3.
ADOPTION_BARRIER: [Token-class labeling at serving time (boilerplate vs value/reasoning) adds a classifier and policy surface; per-class tau tuning doubles the hyperparameter space vs a single global tau; intermediate-LM-head compute overhead not modeled in FLOPs; ragged batching and KV-cache fragmentation from early-exiting tokens; prior-art early-exit (CALM Schuster22, Depth-Adaptive Elbayad20, SkipDecode 23, LayerSkip 24) already provides the global mechanism; tuned global captures ~97% of the benefit with far less complexity; production f and per-class confidence gap are unmeasured (owed) — the analytic model assumes f=0.2-0.35 and a depth gap that may not hold on real traces]
RATIONALE: Packet VERDICT PART B NEGATIVE: "+0.46pp at realistic f, 0/90 clear the 5pp bar (Jensen floor — per-class>=global is definitional; this reproduces the EXP-0006 grammar-region failure mode EXACTLY)". PART A HELD but "delivered by the GLOBAL policy" (+4.56pp agentic vs reasoning at realistic f via best-tuned global, not via structure-aware). SWEEP SUMMARY: by f 0.2->0.44, 0.3->0.48 (mean over grid); best-tuned-global ~10.8% FLOPs saved vs struct ~11.3%. Jensen argument: "per-class >= global is DEFINITIONAL... magnitude is ~0.5pp because a single well-tuned global threshold already captures almost all the structural benefit". Prior-art owed: "CALM (Schuster 2022), Depth-Adaptive Transformer (Elbayad 2020), SkipDecode (2023), LayerSkip (2024)" — novelty is the agentic-structure-conditioned threshold, which dies vs tuned global. LIMITATIONS #3: "REAL wall-clock with early-exit OVERHEAD (intermediate-head compute, batched-exit raggedness, KV-cache implications) — FLOPs-saved overstates wall-clock wins." Actionable negative: use tuned global; skip per-class complexity.
```
